# Project-specific -- mirrors artifact-one-data-quality's split between the
# repo-root .gitignore (generic Python/OS noise, already covers __pycache__,
# .venv, .mypy_cache, etc.) and this file (this project's own generated
# artifacts: dbt build output, Airflow's local metadata DB, and dated
# snapshot files that should never be checked in, while the directory
# structure itself -- and any genuinely checked-in seed content -- stays
# tracked via the .gitkeep exception below).
warehouse/dbt/target/
warehouse/dbt/logs/
warehouse/dbt/dbt_packages/
warehouse/dbt/.user.yml
airflow/logs/
airflow/airflow.db
airflow/airflow.cfg
airflow/webserver_config.py
data_snapshots/*
!data_snapshots/.gitkeep
